title: CLoader Bot Script Host With Double-Extension PDF JavaScript or LuaJIT Interpreter
id: 5e93ba47-1f68-4d72-a0c5-9b48e2f7063d
status: experimental
description: Detects the two execution primitives Seqrite Labs observed in the CLoader bot campaign against Thai organizations. Spear-phishing email attachments arrived as .lha archives named as purchase-order PDFs, expanding to a double-extension .pdf.JS script that Windows resolves through the JavaScript script host, and the loader chain then runs a bundled LuaJIT interpreter with an obfuscated Lua script to conceal its activity. The chain also disabled Microsoft Defender and pulled its C2 response from Pastebin.
references:
  - https://malware.news/t/cloader-bot-campaign-targets-thai-organizations-through-luajit-based-malware-delivery/127554#post_1
  - https://meterpreter.org/cloader-bot-malware-luajit-thailand/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/25
tags:
  - attack.t1566
  - attack.t1204
  - attack.t1059
  - attack.t1027
  - attack.t1562
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_script_host:
    Image|endswith:
      - '\wscript.exe'
      - '\cscript.exe'
  selection_double_extension:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '.pdf.JS'
      - '.pdf.js'
      - '.pdf.Js'
  selection_luajit:
    Image|endswith: '\luajit.exe'
  condition: (selection_script_host and selection_double_extension) or selection_luajit
falsepositives:
  - Mozilla's PDF.js is a legitimate JavaScript library and local copies named pdf.js can be launched through a script host by document-viewing tools
  - Developers and packaging pipelines that run luajit.exe directly
level: medium
